SHPC: {
	TooltipNormal:
		'''
		Consumes Souls as ammo
		Ejects orbs of unstable, concentrated soulpower that linger and explode
		Orbs emit seeking souls and lingering pickup souls after collapse
		Orbs have varying effects depending on Soul type used
		{0}
		Press <right> to use the machine as a vacuum, pulling in lingering souls
		Once released, a torrent of soul lasers is discharged scaling with the number of souls pulled in
		'''
	// These are the soul effect descriptions, the number is the item ID of the soul
	NoSoul: "[c/808080:There is currently no soul type injected into the weapon]"
	SoulDesc520: "[c/F01DC4:Light-infused orbs create larger explosions]"
	SoulDesc521: "[c/7B1DDC:Night-infused orbs create longer lasting explosions]"
	SoulDesc575: "[c/6AF0FA:Flight-infused orbs travel faster and restore flight time on direct hits]"
	SoulDesc548: "[c/0433DE:Might-infused orbs apply mighty knockback to enemies]"
	SoulDesc549: "[c/4FFF7C:Sight-infused orbs seek out nearby enemies]"
	SoulDesc547: "[c/FF6014:Fright-infused orbs deal extra flat damage with their hatred]"
	LegendaryText:
		'''
		'Though soul-powered machines were a near failure, potential remained in souls as a form of fuel.
		To avoid my last experiments' main flaw, the Soul-Harnessing Plasma Cannon was designed to expel souls as projectiles before they exert control over the weapon.
		Each soul type appears to react differently to the base plasma. Yet, lacking volunteers, obtaining potential ammunition is currently too difficult to undergo further testing.
		A shame, for a weapon that could have practically unlimited ammunition in the battlefield. Perhaps some day, its potential can be truly tested.'
		'''
	TooltipGFB: It scales again :)
}

